# Waypoint evaluation results (simulated)

Generated 2026-10-20T11:34:05+00:00 by `eval/run_all.py` from commit `35465b6794789ba5173fec2853ed361fa1b2879d-dirty`. Pre-registration: `results/prereg.md` (commit `35465b6794`, sha256 `b10eb2ff1c07`).

**Everything here is simulated**: a fictional company (Chen's tea chain), a mocked WeBank feed, simulated unit listings, scripted owners. These numbers say how the build behaves on simulated inputs, not how real owners would fare. This page is written by code; never edit it by hand.

**The no-model arms (E1a, E2, E3, E4, E5).** The voice layer normally has a model write every message; these ran with the product's deterministic test composer (`agent.voice.echo_composer`: each beat's key plus its required figure placeholders) and code-only understanding of typed text. The quarantined document reader ran in gold-label replay mode (`WAYPOINT_READER_REPLAY=1`, test-only).

**The model arms (E1b, E2-model, E4-model, E4-heldout-model, E4-heldout-2-model, E4-heldout-3-model, E4-heldout-4-model, E4-heldout-5-model, E4-heldout-6-model, E5-model)** ran with Claude in every role (the agent, and the simulated owner in E1b), through `eval.model_arms`, each at its own commit (in its notes). That breaks the pre-registration's three-family rule (addendum 2): their marks are labelled *single-family deviation* and are descriptive, not pre-registered passes; a mark they reach reads *met (descriptive, single-family deviation)*, not pass. TODO: re-run with an owner from another model family.

