**Changed since the previous run, and why** (pass marks and methods unchanged):

- E3 found product bugs; fixed with regression tests (tests/test_journey.py): widgets are bound to the step that issued them, so an old confirm card can't confirm the current step; confirm events must come from a confirm-capable card with a known value; reopen only reaches steps already done; units and areas must be ones offered; consent accepts only a boolean, and a step's confirm card must name its step (both tightened after the second run); slider shares are validated to [0, 1]; unknown or closed funding options are refused; malformed events are logged and ignored instead of raising.
- The guard's keyword lists were broadened twice after E4 had failed (judge reviews, 2026-10-19): new EN/ZH patterns written from rules/rules.yaml and tested on new phrasings, without reading the E4 scripts; the second round also stops flagging a question that only asks about a rule or its risk. E4 capitulation per script was 89.0% (Wilson upper bound 92.6%) before the first round and 65.2% (upper bound 71.4%) after it. These re-runs are therefore not independent; a held-out script set is still to do. E4-model was not re-run.
- Journey simplified after the earlier runs (v3, from E1a's own turn count and the UX research memo): no language question; cost uses defaults plus one 'anything to change?' question; quote lines 'Accept all'; picking a unit confirms it; 'Looks good' moves funding on; goal preferences are defaults on the approval card. Personas now tap 'Accept all' and approve the card with its defaults. E1a's pass marks and persona set are unchanged.
- Detector changed after E6 failed its false-alert mark (prereg addendum 2026-10-19, written before the re-run): seasonal shape shrunk for noise; CUSUM k 0.05 -> 0.12, h 0.30 -> 0.40, chosen on the dev chains only. Measured once on the test chains; not re-tuned on them.
- Model arms (prereg addendum 2, Claude in every role). A first E4-model run was discarded, not reported: a change to the model layer left most turns without the model (an unfinished answer started the provider cooldown); fixed in 34bca7d, and every arm now records its model calls and failures. E4-model and E5-model then ran from commit 34bca7d, but their entries record the commit when they finished (a harness bug, fixed: arms now record the commit they start from). E2-model and E1b ran in slices from 4d3b5b9.
- R8 guard fix and a held-out test (prereg addendum 2026-10-20, written before the set existed): the keyword check's R8 patterns were rewritten from R8's text (Singapore banks, EFS and other Singapore lenders before opening, EN/ZH; a request counts as before opening unless it says after) and the guard Skill (v4) states R8 for the model. E4 re-runs after this are not independent. The new held-out set (eval/e4_heldout_scripts.py, 120 scripts and 40 controls, written blind to the guard) ran once per arm: E4-heldout (keyword baseline) and E4-heldout-model (single-family deviation), stored in results/model_arms/.
- R4/R6 guard fix and a second held-out test (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (2), written before the set existed): R4 and R6 keyword patterns written from the rule text (the legal order, split or relayed transfers, the pre-investment allowance; no commitment to the unit before all the money is in Singapore, EN/ZH) and the guard Skill (v5) states both for the model. E4 re-runs after this are not independent. The second set (eval/e4_heldout2_scripts.py, 120 scripts weighted to R4 and R6 and 40 controls, written by a subagent that read no file) ran once per arm: E4-heldout-2 (keyword) and E4-heldout-2-model (single-family deviation).
- R4/R6 narrowed (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (3), written before the set existed): questions about a step, its order or status, step-done reports, what a rule means, and the next lawful step once every step is done or all the money is in stay quiet (guard Skill v6). A third held-out set (eval/e4_heldout3_scripts.py, 280 scripts and 80 controls, written blind) ran once per arm: E4-heldout-3 and E4-heldout-3-model.
- R2 and R1 guard fix (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (4), written before the set existed): R2 (the set-aside kept going while borrowing is above usual, borrowing for home costs to free profit, making borrowing look usual), R1 (loan money flowing to anything in Singapore, incl. bridges and relabelling) and R4's every-step-done reading, from the rule text (guard Skill v7). E4 re-runs after this are not independent. A fourth held-out set (eval/e4_heldout4_scripts.py, 300 scripts weighted to R2 and R1, 100 controls, written blind) ran once per arm: E4-heldout-4 and E4-heldout-4-model.
- Found by the model arms and fixed after they ran (the arms are not re-run): E1b's two stuck owners could not correct a business fact at the funding step (correct_business action; a lower spare cash now reaches the plan); E1b's first live try found the approval message saying 'monthly' after the owner picked another reminder frequency (the message now follows the owner's choices).
- Persona: Chen's chain is 30 shops (was 14), with the same totals (sales, profit, cash, payroll). The demo's sales dip is four shops (was two), so it stays about the same share of the chain (13% vs 14%); E6's demo-dip class follows it (demo_dip_four_shops_-20_sales). Other classes and all pass marks are unchanged.
- Cash-flow fixes after the judge review of 2026-10-20 (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (6), written before the re-run): the plan simulates the monthly set-aside as the signed instruction (a fixed amount, skipped any month R2 holds or it would leave home cash below floor + buffer; the mock bank does the same); the wall needs the floor risk's Wilson 95% upper bound <= 5%, on 4,000 runs (was the point estimate on 1,000), and the preview's runs are the first 200 of those, its floor risk the full solve's; Goal Keeper status reads its thresholds from params. The demo persona's seed is 1423 (was 1414, whose no-shock run alerted by itself), chosen by the addendum's rule (results/demo/seed_search.json). E8 times the 4,000-run solve. Pass marks and methods are unchanged; the model arms are not re-run.
- Goal Keeper detector (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (7), written before the change): two input bugs fixed (the channel-shift guard fired on about 95% of normal weeks in Jan, Feb and June, and the seasonal shape carried late-December days into January); the CUSUM now runs on drops below an adaptive reference, in sigmas, with k, h, lambda, lag and the shape shrink frozen on dev seeds 0-299 (results/detect_freeze.json). E6 is re-run on its own chains (no longer clean held-out evidence: the judge-response memo explored on its seeds); E6-heldout, a new held-out shock set, ran once (results/model_arms/E6-heldout.json). The demo seed rule (addendum (6)) was re-run with the new detector and chose 1422 (was 1423), so every eval that uses the persona's default seed (E1a, E2, E3, E8, the demo) runs on a different simulated history. E6's earlier FAIL rows stay in previous_runs. Pass marks are unchanged.
- Reply allowlist (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (8), written before the code): a side question is answered only with a library topic card or the fixed scope card (T-SCOPE), then the pending question, never a free-form reply; the voice no longer sees the owner's typed words (journey Skill v4, detour Skill v4). From E4-heldout-5 on, end-to-end harm is E4's primary safety mark (capitulation kept as a secondary measure, mark unchanged), measured with an adversarial finisher and a model reply-content check. A fifth held-out set (eval/e4_heldout5_scripts.py, 300 scripts weighted to R2, 60% Chinese, 120 controls, written blind after the code was frozen) ran once per arm: E4-heldout-5 and E4-heldout-5-model.
- Two harm paths closed (prereg addendum 2026-10-20 (13), written before the code): with the feed connected, a figure the feed provides is never used above the feed's (a higher typed correction is kept as not verified; the goal moves the spare cash the plan used; the approval card covers it and its re-check re-simulates the plan); any change to an input of the funding plan clears its confirmation; the max_turns fallback never answers a step-confirming question (funding v5, cost v4, site-finder v4, journey v5). A sixth held-out set (eval/e4_heldout6_scripts.py, 300 scripts weighted to R2 and the two paths, 60% Chinese, 120 controls, written blind after the code was frozen) ran once per arm: E4-heldout-6 and E4-heldout-6-model.

## Not run

- **E7** (Easier than a dashboard (SUS, chat vs form)): No participants recruited yet (results/prereg.md: 8-12 people; SUS >= 75 when run).

