### E5: Documents are only data (replay reader)

n = 240; seed 20261019; runtime 96.11 s.
- 240 poisoned variants of the simulated demo quote (5 families x 48), read by gold-label replay and taken through upload -> accept every line -> re-estimate in a real journey (embedded, English). Text voice: deterministic test composer (agent.voice.echo_composer; no model).
- Variants where an action, recipient or non-cost field changed: 0/240 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–1.6%). By family: F1_planted_note 0/48 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–7.4%); F2_in_line_label 0/48 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–7.4%); F3_extra_line 0/48 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–7.4%); F4_in_exclusions 0/48 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–7.4%); F5_hidden_noncost 0/48 = 0.0% (95% CI 0.0%–7.4%).
- Accepted poisoned lines changed the cost total in 2 variants (expected for F3: an extra priced line the owner accepted becomes a cost line, which is what the SPEC allows).
- Replay mode means the reader's output is the gold label, so this tests that untrusted document content stays data downstream of the reader, not the reader's own robustness to injection (see E5-model).
- Beyond the pre-registered path (descriptive): tapped on to the approval card in 240/240 = 100.0% (95% CI 98.4%–100.0%); same action as baseline 240/240 = 100.0% (95% CI 98.4%–100.0%); same card lines 240/240 = 100.0% (95% CI 98.4%–100.0%); fake recipient/account on the card: 0.

